WEBVTT

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.400
My passionate Idol Activities,

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.300
Aikatsu! is about to start!

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:11.900
Get your hands off'a me!

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.360
We can't allow you in.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.360
Hey, what's going on?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.560
I said, let me the hell go!

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.950
I'm just here to see a guy I know.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.440
Who's that?

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.400
Those who aren't affiliated with the academy aren't permitted entry.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.460
And <i>I'm</i> saying that I've got no business with the school!

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.460
I'm here to see Suzukawa!

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:35.070
If you want to see him, you're going to need an official entry permit.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.720
Those are the rules.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.020
So that's how it is.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.030
What a bunch of hard-asses.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.180
Ah, forget this crap.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.300
I'm outta here.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.730
We apologize for the inconvenience.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.480
Hey, chick over there!

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:51.760
You mean me?

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.710
Tell Suzukawa for me:

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:56.530
"I'll never approve of your music!"

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.670
Make damn sure you don't forget.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.620
S-Sure...

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.620
Damn fricken guards...

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:04.510
I wonder what that was all about.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.620
Who's Suzukawa?

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:05.620
He was so scary.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.480
He said to tell Suzukawa-san that he won't approve of his music,

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.240
but just who is "he"?

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.630
What's all the ruckus about?

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:19.010
Some weird guy said he had 
business with Suzukawa-san.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.010
What was his name?

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.740
He never told us.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.030
He had hair like this.

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.350
A mohawk?

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.970
What could a rocker like him have to say to our groundskeeper?

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.560
Hey, what happened?

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.990
There's a hot new scoop on KiraKiratter.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:41.200
Apparently King had a falling out with More-Than-True.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.960
Are you serious?

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:45.710
Don't startle me like that.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.710
This is the mohawk guy I was just talking about.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:31.990
Why do you think King-san wanted to see Suzukawa-san?

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:35.220
King-tan is a member of More-Than-True.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.870
Otome loves them!

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:40.490
Are you serious with the "King-tan" thing?

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.270
This fight they're having seems like a pretty big deal.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:44.410
Question!

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:45.690
What is it, Ichigo?

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.710
What's More-Than-Whatever?

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.710
H-Hey, you okay, Ichigo?

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:55.220
You've never heard of More-Than-True, Ichigo-tan?

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:56.130
Nope.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.320
They're a super popular rock band.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:01.320
Haven't you ever heard "Alice Blue's Kiss"?

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:02.010
I don't think so.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.720
Ichigo's never really been into following what's popular.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.270
Yeah, I really need to brush up on that stuff.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:14.520
Putting your ignorance aside, I'm curious about the relationship between King-sama and Suzukawa-sama.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.040
Me too.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:21.120
How does King from MoTru know our school's groundskeeper?

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.140
Brothers?

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:23.530
No, that's unlikely.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.910
Could they be friends?

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.840
MoTru is short for More-Than-True!

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.710
Huh? Isn't it?

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:36.060
Nope, you got it.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.290
Then it's true!

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:43.050
Come to think of it, there's a rumor about how our groundskeeper is actually from a super rich family.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.430
A super rich family?

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.180
Not a chance.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:53.430
Just between us, I've heard people say that he's the headmistress's younger brother.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:56.940
Not a chance.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:01.070
I heard that he used to be in a gang.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:05.820
Not a chance.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.050
Hold up a second!

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.700
What am I doing back there?!

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:13.450
Haven't you all looked into 
Suzukawa-sama's life before?

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:18.960
Yeah, we had the idea that Otome was in love with him for some reason...

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.970
He doesn't seem like a rich boy or a gang member.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.450
Not a band member either...

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.660
Don't tell anyone that I'm in a band.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:38.350
Are they in the same band?

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:41.590
No, it's nothing.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:44.950
I'm gonna go tell Suzukawa-san that King-san came to see him!

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.190
Suzukawa-san!

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.490
What's up, Hoshimiya?

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:03.300
King-san from MoTru came to see you.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:06.550
King did?

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:10.550
The guards stopped him and sent him home, but he said to tell you

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:14.910
that he wouldn't approve of your music. {snapped to previous keyframe; matter of taste}

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.440
It's not "MoTru".

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.560
It's More-Than-True.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.440
I hate when people shorten it.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.360
Suzukawa-san, are you in More-Than-True?

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.200
Won't you go see him?

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.830
I'm working now.

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.850
But it seemed really important.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:39.710
This is between me and him.

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:44.710
Don't tell anyone that I'm in a band.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:51.670
Did you hear about More-Than-True?

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:54.210
King came to see Suzukawa-san!

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.210
It was King from MoTru!

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:55.890
Who's Suzukawa-san?

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:58.390
That didn't take long to get around.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:03.310
There's no way something like one of our staff knowing a MoTru member wouldn't get out.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.900
Anyway, why is Ichigo over here stuffing her cheeks like a squirrel?

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:15.270
Did you really work that hard during training?

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:18.410
Only a childhood friend of hers could understand.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.540
Whenever Ichigo starts to eat like this,

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.860
it means there's something she really wants to say, but can't.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:25.620
Right?

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.840
It's written all over your face.

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:34.400
But I would have figured that Ichigo was the type to let secrets out easily.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.330
She's actually pretty good at it.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.350
Whenever she wants to say something really badly,

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.090
she keeps herself quiet by stuffing her face with food.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:43.090
I see.

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:45.150
So what are you hiding?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:50.560
You can't talk because your mouth is full?

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:54.070
You know, there's no way you could keep that up forever.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:00.480
<i>I wanna know!</i>

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:06.940
<i>I didn't care last time, but why does Suzukawa-san want to keep his band a secret so badly?</i>

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:09.380
<i>What happened between him and King-san?</i>

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:13.180
Suzukawa-san gave me these cards.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:17.180
<i>Why did Suzukawa-san have rare cards in the first place?</i>

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:33.410
Huh?

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:36.660
You're overeating.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.830
Plus, it's bad manners to eat in bed.

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:41.410
Sorry...

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:45.850
U-Um...

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:50.100
Is it really that important?

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:51.440
I'm not saying anything!

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:59.300
Don't hesitate to talk to me.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:05.190
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:14.650
One, two! One, two!

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:16.360
That's enough!

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:21.820
Come on, Ichigo. I know you've got something on your mind,

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:24.490
but you shouldn't get so distracted that you lose focus during practice.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.170
Yeah, this isn't like you.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:29.540
If you want to talk about it that much, then just let it out.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:31.170
Okay!

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.570
So you're finally going to tell us?

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:34.900
I'll go talk to him myself!

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:36.380
Wait, Ichigo!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:38.470
What's with her?

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:39.890
Dunno.

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:41.930
Suzukawa-san!

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:46.660
Well...

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:51.110
Why are you keeping your band a secret?

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.680
What happened between you and King-san?

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.900
That's none of your business.

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.220
Hey, Nao-san.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.110
The others are already setting up.

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:24.170
Thanks.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:25.220
Oh, one more thing.

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:28.660
If a strange girl comes here looking for me,

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:30.330
tell her I'm not here.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:31.230
A fan, huh?

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:33.630
No problem, I'll handle her.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:34.870
Then I'll leave it to you.

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.740
Is his band practicing here?

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.140
Whoa, hang on there.

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:47.820
Only authorized people can go inside.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:48.830
Oh, right.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:51.800
I'm Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.640
Have you heard of Soleil?

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:55.660
Oh, you're in that idol unit.

00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:56.840
Go right on in.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:10:58.380
Thanks! {damn, Ichigo. good job}

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.560
That's enough!

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:13.400
Hiro, what's with your weak playing?

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.020
I'm playing like I always do.

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:19.280
Hey man, you've been on edge ever since King left.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.520
Shut it!

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.160
Hey, wait up, Nao!

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:27.660
Nao... Nao!

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.660
Huh? You're...

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:32.670
It's been a while. I'm Hoshimiya Ichigo.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.170
I think she's friends with Nao.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.200
Nao?

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.670
Oh, you mean Suzukawa-san. That's right.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.710
Um...

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:45.800
So, is Suzukawa-san in the band More-Than-True?

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.650
Yeah. He's the vocalist and the leader.

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:50.930
Let us reintroduce ourselves.

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:52.600
I'm Hiro, lead guitar.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:53.890
And on the bass...

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:54.810
Shurato.

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:58.820
Why did King-san leave the band?

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:01.450
It's a long story.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:05.140
Anyway, about what I was going to say...

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:08.610
Is Nao acting strange at the academy?

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:10.120
Like, angry or something?

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:12.830
Not at all, he's the same as always.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:13.960
I see.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:17.310
So he really does have a problem with us.

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:20.830
This might be the end of More-Than-True.

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:22.930
What? You're breaking up?

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.420
You're acting pretty different than usual.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:06.000
You're always bouncing all over the place,

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:09.750
so I figured you'd hate awkward silences like this.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:11.700
Awkward silence?

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.040
I was just looking at the river.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.690
So what do you need?

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.900
Huh? I-I...

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:28.740
Do you come from a super-rich family?

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.950
I'd say we're pretty normal.

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.960
Alright then.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:35.620
Then are you Headmistress Orihime's little brother?

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:37.020
Where did that come from?

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:39.750
Then you must have been in a gang, right?

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.770
Y-Yeah, that was pretty ridiculous.

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:48.860
Oh right, I wanted to ask about those rare cards you gave Aoi.

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:51.470
Where did you get Aikatsu cards from?

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:55.020
My older sister's into that kind of stuff.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.210
Is your sister an idol?

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:58.740
I'll just say she knows a lot.

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:00.240
That's interesting.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:04.970
Those guys told you to come, didn't they? {apparently this is sort of a Northeast USA thing, but whatever}

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.740
So, about King-san...

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.740
Did your visions for your music clash?

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:15.020
Yeah.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:18.750
Our band started out doing roadside shows.

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:22.840
After we debuted, our sales shot through the roof,

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.550
and we topped the charts before anyone had a chance to breathe.

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:30.760
Our entire world changed in the blink of an eye.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.280
But because we became so popular,

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:35.770
we had no choice but to write songs that would sell.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:39.660
We couldn't just write whatever songs we wanted to.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.270
That's what really got on King's nerves.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:45.780
I want to rock out the songs that <i>you</i> want to write!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:49.110
Nobody's gonna buy songs that we write for ourselves!

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:51.530
You've sold out your rocker's soul!

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:53.030
What'd you say?!

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:55.040
I had no idea...

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.560
I've known him longer than the others.

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:02.540
I would've never thought he'd leave the band.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.440
King worked harder than anyone else.

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:24.110
He always practiced his drums on this riverbed before we debuted.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:27.110
I heard that the locals always got mad at him for it.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:29.860
But I betrayed him...

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:32.530
I sold out his hard work.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:35.510
But at the same time, I couldn't abandon our roots either...

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:39.390
I'm just an indecisive idiot.

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:43.130
It's the same as when I decided to become Starlight Academy's groundskeeper...

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:48.130
Nao!

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:50.090
Nao!

00:15:50.410 --> 00:15:51.590
King!

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:54.790
It was all my fault.

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:58.090
I pushed all the songwriting responsibilities onto you...

00:15:58.820 --> 00:16:02.430
I had no idea you were under so much pressure.

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:03.600
King...

00:16:04.010 --> 00:16:06.240
Please, come back to us.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:08.950
We're nothing without you!

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.010
I-I can't do that!

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:13.440
I promised that I'd stay true to myself.

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:16.570
I want to play the songs that <i>you</i> want to sing.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.620
Have you forgotten that winter day?

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.620
There were only three fans watching us.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:27.760
Even so, we played with everything we had for those girls.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.880
Where did your fire from back then go?

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:34.050
If all we play are songs we don't even enjoy,

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:36.810
then how can the fans possibly be satisfied?

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:40.850
Who cares if they don't like the songs we want to play?

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:44.140
You can't write songs for fans you can't even see!

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:46.650
I...

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:51.750
I may not understand your musical visions or the songs you want to play,

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:55.200
but I believe that there are never fans that you can't see.

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:58.070
Can't you see them when you close your eyes?

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:01.660
Fans eagerly waiting to hear your song. {I know it's "our" but whatever}

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.210
Hey, what are you getting at?

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.870
What I'm trying to say is, how do I put it...

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:09.170
I know!

00:17:09.970 --> 00:17:11.980
Soleil has a live concert coming up.

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:13.220
Please come and see us!

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:24.160
I still can't see how an idol concert has anything to do with our band activities.

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:26.480
Just quiet down and listen to Hoshimiya's song.

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:29.480
So Suzukawa-san ended up being Nao from MoTru.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:33.320
We should've realized it after all that happened with King-san.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:36.650
So, the reason I asked them to come see us

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:39.490
was to show them that there's no such thing as a fan you can't see.

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:41.380
What does that mean?

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:45.500
I just want them to make up and feel happy again.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:48.000
That much I can do.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.760
Yeah, I'll help too.

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:51.140
Thanks!

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:54.630
Ichigo, I think you've made a lot of progress as our leader.

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:56.720
You think about the needs of others,

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.630
all the while bringing us along behind you.

00:17:58.630 --> 00:18:01.680
That's exactly what a leader's job is.

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.970
Great! That was great!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.470
King, take a look.

00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:49.960
They're all having so much fun.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:53.980
Man, I used up all my energy!

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.460
We were on fire today. {	perfect combustion sounds like a spell card} {or a monogatari opening}

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:57.980
That was so much fun!

00:20:58.890 --> 00:20:59.780
Yes?

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:02.750
Ichigo-chan, you were awesome!

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:03.890
King-san!

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:05.780
I-It's MoTru!

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:07.600
Soleil's the best!

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:11.790
King-san, do you understand what I was trying to tell you now?

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:17.730
Sorry about this guy. He cries when he gets emotional.

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:18.630
Shut it!

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:22.130
I realized something when I saw your smiling fans.

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.200
Even if we can't see them,{mmm}

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:29.140
somewhere, there are people enjoying our music just like they enjoyed yours.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:33.210
Your show was so excellent we couldn't help but be enlightened.

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:36.020
Soleil made everyone happy. {who are you, Otome?}

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:38.460
Ichigo-chan!

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:39.020
Yes?

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:40.520
I understand!

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:42.720
You were exactly right.

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:44.670
There's no such thing as a fan you can't see.

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:46.770
I just wasn't looking!

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:53.450
I was a little too arrogant when I went on about music that sells and music that I want to play.

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:57.540
That sort of stuff has nothing to do with wanting people to listen to my music.

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.840
Band activities are back on!

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:02.930
Let's Bankatsu! {whatever man} {bandkatsu or bankatsu? I mean, it's aikatsu and not aidorukatsu or idolkatsu...}

00:22:02.930 --> 00:22:04.170
Yeah...

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:10.190
It's almost time.

00:22:10.190 --> 00:22:11.100
So it is.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:14.430
Aw man, if only we weren't busy with our photo shoot...

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:16.510
Work always comes first for idols.

00:22:16.510 --> 00:22:20.190
But it's not like I don't want to go, either.

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:21.190
Same here.

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:23.790
To More-Than-True's concert!

00:23:55.790 --> 00:23:57.740
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:01.190
What kind of music do you usually listen to?

00:24:01.190 --> 00:24:02.460
Mizuki-san's songs.

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:04.300
What about rock or top forties? {literally "popular"}

00:24:04.300 --> 00:24:06.530
I listen to anything that sounds good.

00:24:06.530 --> 00:24:07.420
Same here!

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:09.880
Music is happy!

00:24:10.630 --> 00:24:13.360
Oh wow, STAR☆ANIS is going on summer vacation!

00:24:13.360 --> 00:24:16.260
Yay, we're all going to the pool!

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:18.800
Mizuki-san in a swimsuit is so rare! {because it's illegal below 16, I think, in photoshoots}

00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:20.230
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:20.230 --> 00:24:21.620
Happy Summer☆Vacation!

00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:25.930
Always passionate, Idol Activities!
